<spell-notebook "input theming">
	<header level="1">
		Input
		<header>An input is a field used to elicit a response from a user.</>
	</>
	<input-tab-bar showing="theming"/>
	<section>
		<html>
			<ui-menu class="ui-docs-section-tabs" appearance="segmented" aria-label="Sections">
				<ui-item link="#tokens">Tokens</>
				<ui-item link="#themes">Themes</>
			</>
		</>
	</>

	<!-- THEMING:  the family's tokens, live, plus how to set them and which themes touch it. -->
	<section label="Tokens">
		<markdown>
			Theme with the public `--ui-input-*` tokens: set one on the element, on any ancestor (a form, `:root`), or on the
			root box through `::part(input)`. They inherit into the shadow root, where the sheet reads each through a private
			alias, so nothing inside blocks them.

			- `<ui-textarea>` reads the same set.
			- Style the native control itself with `::part(control)`.
		</>
		<markdown>
			```css
			ui-input,
			ui-textarea {
			  --ui-input-radius: 0;
			  --ui-input-border-color-focus: var(--ui-primary);
			}
			ui-input::part(control) {
			  font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
			}
			```
		</>
		<message state="info" size="small">
			<markdown>
				A `state` swaps in its own border and background colours over yours. Never set the `--_ui-input-*` names:
				they're the sheet's private plumbing.
			</>
		</>
		<markdown>Edit a value below to try it.</>
		<html>
			<ui-docs-tokens family="ui-input" playground>
				<ui-input placeholder="Search..." aria-label="Search"></>
			</>
		</>
	</>

	<section label="Themes">
		<markdown>
			The theme menu above picks the theme for every page of the site:  Spell, Glass, Fruity or Merlot,
			each restyling this component through its tokens.
		</>
	</>
</spell-notebook>
